tializeState at index 0 resets receipts dir and state, and the suite always runs index 0 first, fail-closed is correct (better than silently inheriting ambient env). Judge: acceptable.\n\nNow, does anything else in the walker use `Deno.env.get`? Check suite test and permission grants: the walker script runs with `--allow-env=PATH` only. Does readme-command.ts import anything needing more env? `resolveResourceUrlsFromAppHost` — that's in-process, no env. `Deno.mkdir`, `Deno.remove`, `Deno.writeTextFile` — need write perms (granted broad). runAspireCommand spawns Deno.Command — needs --allow-run (granted broad). OK.\n\nWait — one more: does the walker also need `--allow-env` for anything else... `Deno.env.get('PATH')` only. And `Deno.Command` with explicit `env` — when `env` is passed to Deno.Command, does it replace the whole environment or merge? Per Deno docs: \"env: Environment variables to set for the command. By default, the command inherits the parent environment\" — actually with `env` specified, it's merged over the inherited env (clearEnv defaults false). The brief says \"merged over inherited env via Deno.Command({ env })\" — correct: Deno.Command env option adds/overrides on top of inherited env unless clearEnv: true. Good — ambient PATH tail survives, `aspire`/`deno`/`curl` resolve from ambient PATH.\n\nHmm wait — important nuance: they OVERRIDE PATH entirely: `PATH: <prepend><DELIMITER><ambient PATH>`. They set PATH (merged over inherited — same value). Good, that keeps ambient tail.\n\nNow check aspire-walk.ts full file for the runAspireCommand and other functions (runQuickstartWalk?), and quickstart.walk unchanged (env optional). Read it.\n\nAlso check the suite file readmeWalkerCommand context, and the domain file for expected commands, substitution, and README.md quickstart block to understand test indexes (index 1 = ?).","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":