k. Worth a note.\n\nAlso `readmeCommandEnvironment` reads ambient PATH each spawn — later indexes get fresh ambient PATH; fine and desirable.\n\nItem 8 also asks: does readState rejecting prior-run state lacking denoInstallRoot count as fail-closed and correct? Yes: initializeState at index 0 resets both state and receipts; any ≥1 index always follows a successful index 0 within the same PR version. A pre-upgrade persisted state (from an older commit) at `.llm/tmp/readme-quickstart/state.json` on the runner would be rejected with \"malformed prior run receipt\" → gate fails closed rather than silently running with ambient env → correct. Note: the state file lives at repoRoot/.llm/tmp/readme-quickstart/state.json — could a stale state.json from a PREVIOUS canary run (pre-fix) exist on the hosted runner? If so, command 1 (index 0) calls initializeState which... does NOT delete the state file itself! It deletes `.deno-install` and the receipts dir, then returns fresh state and — wait, does index 0 overwrite state.json? Only on success: `writeState(statePath, nextState)` after result.code===0. But the stale-file problem: at index 0, state is NOT read (initializeState ignores it) — so a stale pre-fix state.json is simply ignored and overwritten on success. Good, no issue.\n\nBut hmm — one more: at index 0, if the command FAILS, state.json isn't written (stale remains) — but the gate already failed. Fine.\n\nNow item 5: \"no broader env grant\" — the walker command grants `--allow-read`, `--allow-write`, `--allow-run`, `--allow-env=PATH`. Confirm no `--allow-env` elsewhere in the suite file and that the suite test asserts it. The suite test asserts `commands.every((command) => command.includes('--allow-env=PATH'))` — presentation test line 67. Let me get exact line numbers for evidence: readme-quickstart-suite.ts line for '--allow-env=PATH' and the test line. Also check there's no other spawn in the suite granting env more broadly — grep '--allow-env' in the suite file.\n